  "description": "Avalonia controls that ship as types only — no styling of their own. Currently: CalendarView, a single-control calendar replacing Avalonia's five-part built-in family (inline month view with month/year/decade zoom, single or range selection with hover preview, event-dot markers, keyboard navigation, and an optional picker presentation from the same control), backed by the pure-logic CalendarSelectionEngine. Appearance is deliberately left to the consuming theme: every visual detail reaches the control through pseudo-classes and templated parts, so any theme styles it exactly like a stock Avalonia control. This mirrors how first-party Avalonia controls are split — types in the framework, look owned by the theme package — which is what lets these controls be absorbed into the framework later without touching the themes that style them.",
